{
  "id": "5-10-defender-7-lab-waves",
  "title": "5.10.7 Lab: Waves",
  "description": "Enemies stop arriving on a beat and come in waves instead: each wave only after the field is clear and a pause has run out, each one bigger and faster. Write nextWave and spawnWave, and start every round at wave 0.",
  "type": "lesson",
  "estimateMins": 18,
  "category": "Unit 2: moSHion: Applied Game Development",
  "unit": "5.10 Project: Defender, Part B",
  "preview": "moshion",
  "week": 12,
  "slos": [
    "SLO-3"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "title": "A round starts at wave 0",
      "instructions": "`spawnOnBeat()` is gone: enemies now come in waves. The top of the screen says `wave: undefined`, running into `base:` beside it, because nothing sets the wave yet. In `startRound()`, set `wave` to 0 and `wavePause` to 60, so every round, the first one and every one after R, starts with a one-second pause before wave 1. Run it: the top should read `wave: 0`.",
      "hints": [
        "`wave = 0;` and `wavePause = 60;`, beside the other lines that put a round back.",
        "`startRound()` is called by `setup()` and by the R key, so one place covers both."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "title": "Count down on a clear field",
      "instructions": "In `nextWave()`, return straight away while any enemies are left. Otherwise count `wavePause` down by 1, and when it reaches 0 call `spawnWave()` and set `wavePause` back to 90. This is 5.10.6's `nextWave()`, word for word.",
      "hints": [
        "`if (enemies.length > 0) return;` is the first line.",
        "The countdown is Part A's cooldown under another name: take 1 off every frame, and act at 0."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "title": "Build a wave",
      "instructions": "In `spawnWave()`, add 1 to `wave` and set `fallSpeed` to `0.5 + wave * 0.25`, so each wave falls a little faster. Then loop `wave + 2` times. On loop number `i` the enemy is tough (3 hp) when `i % 3 === 2` and has 1 hp otherwise; build it with `spawnEnemy(40 + floor(random(8)) * 45, -20 - i * 50, hp)`, which stacks the wave above the top in a staggered line, each at a random spot across the screen. Play to wave 3, then press R in the middle of a wave: the field should empty, `wave:` should read 0, and wave 1 should come again after the pause.",
      "hints": [
        "`const hp = i % 3 === 2 ? 3 : 1;` makes every third enemy a tough one.",
        "`-20 - i * 50` puts each enemy 50 pixels above the one before it, so they come down one after another."
      ]
    }
  ],
